<title>BELGIUM: Belgian GBL warrant raises 3.47 bln Bfr.</title>
<headline>Belgian GBL warrant raises 3.47 bln Bfr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Groupe Bruxelles Lambert SA said in a statement on Tuesday it had raised 3.471 billion francs in fresh capital through the exercise of warrants on its shares.</p>
<p>The warrants exercise had led to the creation of 788,881 new shares, which would be fungible with existing shares from Wednesday, GBL said.</p>
<p>GBL said there were still 1,485,938 warrants on its share in circulation. The warrants can be exercised twice a year in June and December until 1998 at a price of 4,400 francs.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
